{"timestamp": 1779341164.891158, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 17, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779341182.312486, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Alice's body down in lower engine. Here's what happened: I was passing through upper engine earlier and saw both Alice and Eve there. Right around tick 10, I saw both of them leave upper engine and head south towards lower engine together. I went up to oxygen to do my task, and when I finally made my way down to lower engine, Alice was dead. \n\nEve, you were the last person I saw with her heading exactly to where she died. You have a lot of explaining to do. Has anyone else seen Eve since then?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779341192.4468398, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank, your story lines up perfectly with what I saw. I started on the right side of the map\u2014security, weapons, navigation\u2014and then made my way to storage. \n\nAt tick 15, I saw Eve enter storage directly from lower engine. She stayed in storage with me until the meeting was called. If you saw her heading into lower engine with Alice around tick 10, and she came out alone at tick 15 without reporting a body, that looks incredibly suspicious for Eve. I'd really like to hear Eve explain what happened in lower engine. Right now, she's my top suspect based on the timeline."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341200.5896764, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank, I can actually back up part of your timeline. We were both in Medbay early on, around ticks 3 to 5. Right at tick 5, I saw Eve leave Medbay and head straight for Upper Engine. If you saw her and Alice there around tick 10, and then Bob saw her coming out of Lower Engine alone at tick 15... this looks really, really bad for Eve. \n\nEve, you went exactly where Frank said you did, and you came out exactly where Bob said you did. Unless you have a bulletproof explanation for what happened in Lower Engine, my vote is going on you."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341216.0757115, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I spent most of this round on my own, moving from navigation through security, electrical, and medbay, and I had just arrived in upper engine when the meeting was called. \n\nI didn't see the crime scene, but I *can* completely verify Bob's alibi for the early game. I was in the area and saw Bob leaving security towards navigation right around tick 6. Since Bob was exactly where he claimed to be, I fully trust his sighting of Eve at tick 15.\n\nWhen you put it all together, the evidence is pretty damning. Charlie tracked Eve to upper engine, Frank saw her go into lower engine with Alice, and my cleared player (Bob) saw her leave lower engine alone without reporting the body. \n\nEve, three different people have you pinned at every stage of this murder. Unless you've got an absolute miracle of an explanation, my vote is going on you."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341232.4541204, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Whoa, everyone, please hold on and think about this logically before you vote! I am not denying the timeline, but you're misinterpreting what happened. \n\nYes, Charlie, I went from Medbay to Upper Engine. Yes, Frank, Alice and I were in Upper Engine and we walked down to Lower Engine together around tick 10. I'm not hiding that at all because I have nothing to hide! We both had tasks in Lower Engine. I finished my task quickly and headed into Storage, where Bob saw me arrive at tick 15. \n\nHere's the critical missing piece: **Alice was perfectly fine and alive when I left Lower Engine.** \n\nThink about Frank's story. He admits he was in Upper Engine watching us. He claims he went to Oxygen, but nobody has verified that. He knew exactly where Alice and I went. It is incredibly easy for Frank to have waited a moment, followed us down to Lower Engine, killed Alice after I left for Storage, and then self-reported to frame me using the fact that I was the last person seen with her. \n\nFrank is self-reporting to set up an easy misdirection. Bob, you know I came to Storage and just chilled with you. If I had just killed someone, why would I walk directly into you and hang around? I left her alive. Frank is the one who found the body because he's the one who created it. I'm voting Frank, and if you vote me, you're giving the Duck exactly what they want."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341260.9804275, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Eve, that's a desperate defense. You admit you were with Alice right before she died, and Charlie and Bob have both tracked your exact movements which line up perfectly with my report. I had tasks to do, which is why I went to oxygen, and when I came down, she was dead. You're the one who was last seen with her, heading into the exact room where her body was found. I'm voting for you, and I urge everyone else to do the same before you pick us off one by one."}}
